// =====================================================================================================================================
// File          : EntsTestData.java
// Package       : utilities
// Description   : Runtime test data for the ENTS (Transfer of Entitlements) test cases.
//
//                 Replaces the herd numbers and names that were typed into the ENTS feature files. The feature file now
//                 carries a token such as {transferor.herd}; the step that creates the transfer asks this class for a
//                 fresh pair of herds, and every later step in the same section reads the same pair.
//
//                 How a pair is picked (same-agent transfers):
//                   1. The Agent Login query runs ONCE per agent per run on the ENTS_DATA connection (DBRouter "ENTS").
//                      Up to ents.pool.size rows come back in random order and are kept in memory for the whole run.
//                   2. The rows are shuffled again, and every herd already listed in the used-herds file is skipped.
//                   3. The first unused herd becomes the transferor, the next unused herd becomes the transferee.
//                   4. Both herds are written to the used-herds file straight away, so a failed run does not hand the
//                      same (possibly half-transferred) herds to the next run.
//
//                 Tokens understood by resolve():
//                   {transferor.herd}  {transferor.name}  {transferor.address}
//                   {transferee.herd}  {transferee.name}  {transferee.address}
//                   {agent}              - the transferor agent (the logged-in agent)
//                   {transferee.agent}   - the transferee's agent; the same as {agent} for a same-agent transfer
//                   {transferor.agent}   - same as {agent}
//                   {transferee.login}   - the user who logs in to accept: the transferee agent, or the individual's own
//                                          login for an agent-to-individual transfer (TC_05_ENTS / TC_06_ENTS)
//                   {transferor.login}   - the user who creates the transfer: the agent, or the individual's own login
//                                          when the transferor is an individual (TC_08 / TC_09 / TC_10_ENTS)
//                   {auto.agent}         - the agent with the MOST usable herds, other than the logged-in agent
//                                          (01-10-2026). Use it in the transfereeAgent row and in the re-login step
//                                          instead of hard-coding an agent with few herds (aga6325 has 5). Picked once
//                                          per scenario, so every step of the scenario gets the same agent. Ranking:
//                                          vault stock (ENTS_AGENT pools), else the ranking TC_00_DATA stored, else
//                                          the live query "ENTS Top agents". Expired logins are skipped.
//                   {auto.agent.2}       - the second best agent, {auto.agent.3} the third, and so on
//                 Any other value is returned unchanged, so a feature file can still pin a herd for debugging.
//
//                 Negative case (TC_02_ENTS Section 2): nextNoEntitlementPair picks the transferor from the agent's herds
//                 that hold NO entitlements (query "ENTS Agent herds without entitlements") and the transferee from the
//                 usual Agent Login pool. The same tokens are used.
//
//                 Cross-agent transfers (TC_04_ENTS): nextCrossAgentPair picks the transferor from the logged-in agent's
//                 Agent Login pool and the transferee from the OTHER agent's pool (one query per agent, cached for the
//                 run). {transferee.agent} then returns the other agent, for the login-swap step.
//
//                 Agent-to-individual transfers (TC_05_ENTS / TC_06_ENTS): nextAgentToIndividualPair picks the transferor
//                 from the logged-in agent's Agent Login pool and the transferee from the Individual Login query (herds
//                 whose holder has their own online login). {transferee.login} returns that individual's login.
//
//                 Individual as transferor (TC_08_ENTS / TC_09_ENTS / TC_10_ENTS): the login step runs BEFORE the create
//                 step, so the pair is built in two halves. nextIndividualTransferor picks the individual (herd + login)
//                 and makes it the current pair with NO transferee yet; {transferor.login} logs that individual in. The
//                 create step then completes the pair with completePairWithAgentTransferee (a client herd of the named
//                 agent, TC_08 / TC_10) or completePairWithIndividualTransferee (another individual, TC_09).
//
//                 Pinned transferor (TC_11_ENTS): nextTransfereeForFixedTransferor keeps a transferor herd typed in the
//                 feature file and picks only the transferee from the named agent's pool.
//
//                 Settings (application.properties):
//                   ents.pool.size          - rows fetched per query (default 200)
//                   ents.skip.used.herds    - true = never reuse a herd listed in the used-herds file (default true)
//                   ents.used.herds.file    - the used-herds file (default runtime-data/ents_used_herds.csv)
//                   ents.scheme.year        - only herds with entitlements in this year (blank = all years)
//                   ents.cust.type          - only herds of this customer type, e.g. Individual (blank = all types)
//                   ents.name.two.words     - true = only herds whose DB name is exactly two words (default true)
//                   ents.individual.pool.size - rows fetched by the Individual Login query (default ents.pool.size)
//
// Author        : Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
// Date Created  : 22-09-2026 | Updated: 23-09-2026 (nextNoEntitlementPair for TC_02_ENTS)
//                                       29-09-2026 (nextCrossAgentPair and {transferee.agent} for TC_04_ENTS)
//                                       30-09-2026 (nextAgentToIndividualPair and {transferee.login} for TC_05/06_ENTS)
//                                       30-09-2026 (individual transferor, two-half pairs, pinned transferor: TC_07 to TC_11_ENTS)
//                                       01-10-2026 (Test Data Vault: pools come from utilities.TestDataVault when TC_00_DATA
//                                                   filled it; the live query stays as the fallback and refills the vault)
//                                       06-10-2026 (ETF authorisation, TC_14_ENTS: etfLogins / setEtf and the tokens
//                                                   {etf.code} and {etf.partner} - the ETF picked at random from the
//                                                   dropdown and the login of that ETF's partner)
//
//                 Test Data Vault (01-10-2026): agentPool / noEntitlementPool / individualPool first look in the vault
//                 (pools ENTS_AGENT / ENTS_NO_ENTS / ENTS_INDIVIDUAL). When the vault has AVAILABLE rows for the pool they
//                 are used and the query is NOT run; when it has none, the query runs exactly as before and its rows are
//                 also stored in the vault for the next run. Every herd handed out is marked RESERVED in the vault,
//                 markNotFound marks it BAD with the reason, and markCurrentPairUsed (called by the submit step) marks
//                 both herds USED. Three BAD herds in a row from one pool make the pool refetch itself (live query).
// =====================================================================================================================================

